# Breadcrumbs

Breadcrumbs explain a page’s place in a hierarchy and provide routes to its parents.

These are civica.uk reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use them on a multi-level reference site or administrative information page. The visible page heading identifies the current page; the trail can list its parents.

## When not to use it

Do not use them for a linear setup journey or pair them with a back link. They show hierarchy, not a record of recently visited dashboards.

## Home Assistant adaptation

Home Assistant’s sidebar and native navigation already supply much of this context. Add breadcrumbs only where a deeper hierarchy needs them, such as a device detail flow. Use real parent routes and preserve ordinary link behaviour; do not invent an extra hierarchy from entity identifiers.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Use a labelled navigation landmark and an ordered list. Keep link text understandable out of context. The shared GOV.UK reference permits wrapping; a condensed mobile parent link requires its own tested implementation rather than silently removing destinations.

